Reach the host's plugins from the web client

Settings > Plugins listed nothing in the tile and its enable, consent and panel
controls did nothing at all - no error, no effect - while the same host showed
every installed plugin on desktop.

`window.api.plugins` was absent from the web preload, so each member fell through
`createFallbackProxy` and resolved to `undefined`. The wire already exists:
v1.4.190 split `main/plugins/plugin-client-list.ts` out of `ipc/plugins.ts`
specifically so `plugins.list` RPC could reach it without `ipcMain`, and
`main/index.ts` installs the plugin service through `setPluginServiceForRpc`
inside `app.whenReady()` - the shared startup path `orca serve` runs. Both routes
execute through PluginService's single chokepoint, so a permission decision
cannot differ between a local window and a paired client.

Six of the twenty-one members have a runtime method. The rest - install, the
marketplace surfaces, logs and refresh - exist only as `ipcMain` handlers
upstream, so they are deliberately left off this object: `withFallback` resolves
missing keys per key, which keeps their present behaviour rather than turning a
silent `undefined` into a rejection, and it already answers an `on*` name with a
no-op unsubscribe, which `onChanged` needs in order to stay synchronous. So this
restores listing, enabling, consent and the panel bridge; installing a plugin
from the tile still needs a wire upstream does not have.

No allowlist change: `plugins.*` mutates host state and stays off
`MOBILE_RPC_METHOD_ALLOWLIST`, where upstream already leaves it. That is now
asserted rather than assumed - every other family this series routes pins itself
off the allowlist with a negative case, and plugins was the one that did not.

What still holds the pane back is not `install`. `PluginsSettingsSection` guards
its list effect on `settings.pluginSystemEnabled`, and that key is on neither
`SettingsUpdate` nor the settings-sync allowlist, so the tile's master switch
flips a browser-local boolean and none of the six methods above is ever called.
Routing that one key to the host - as its own runtime-scope method, never by
widening `SettingsUpdate`, which a paired phone reaches - is what makes this pane
work, and it also turns on plugin panels in the right sidebar and plugin quick
commands. It is not in this patch.

To test, open Settings > Plugins in the tile and turn the plugin system on: the
host's plugins should list and a toggle should stick across a reload. Until
`pluginSystemEnabled` reaches the host that switch does not persist, so the direct
route is `plugins.list` and `plugins.setEnabled` over `window.api.plugins`.
Installing a plugin from the tile still throws - `install`, `refresh` and `remove`
have no runtime method. Red with this patch popped:
`web-plugins-bridge.test.ts`. `mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts` stays green popped -
it is a patched file, so popping deletes its two plugin cases rather than failing
them; they guard the allowlist, they do not cover this patch.
